{
  "_comment": "wq#4688 — design/orchestrator_verify_lane.md S3 option B + S6. Standalone settings file for the ops-apply LANE (fworker.resolve_worker_settings selects it by ticket lane, not archetype or repo, and it replaces the per-repo repos.d/ union outright, like verify-probe.json). A ticket only reaches a worker with this file after harness/ops_apply_lane.py's six spawn gates passed (manifest, report, judge PASS, precheck, backup, target). The ONLY mutation paths are the two broker verbs `fleet-exec apply-staged` and `fleet-exec docker-exec-allowlisted` (plus the `restart` they pin), whose every operand is pinned in the 0444 grant.json the spawner mints; this file therefore allows no editor-of-the-world: no python3/node/sed/awk/find/cp/mv/tee/curl/lumen-run (each can write files or open a second mutation path), no raw git apply/checkout/reset/restore/stash/push, no docker, no sudo, no systemctl beyond read verbs. Writes: reports/** in the worker's own worktree only. Bare Write/Edit are absent from allow (acceptEdits auto-approves edits not explicitly denied), so every PRIMARY tree and every home-root path is denied explicitly below in addition to guard.sh's PRIMARY_TREES wall. action_gate runs in its default (non-enforce) mode on purpose: FOREMAN_JUDGE_ENFORCE=1 lets a judge LOOSEN a RED, and the judge's say for this lane is already spent at spawn (gate 2), bound to the exact report + manifest.",
